statement:
Numbers $1$, $2$, ..., $n$ are placed in a row in a certain order. We are allowed to do the following operation: take any two pairs of consecutive elements, that have no common elements, and exchange their positions. Is it possible to get a monotone sequence of elements after a finite number of steps if:

a) $n = 2009$;
b) $n = 2010$?

Find all functions such that $f: \mathbb{Z} \to \mathbb{Z}$ that satisfy the following two conditions:
1) $f(x + f(x + 2y)) = f(2x) + f(2y)$ for all integers $x, y$;
2) $f(0) = 2$.
